  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 228 PM EDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nLargely a persistence forecast as we remain on the eastern periphery \nof an anomalous ridge axis centered in vicinity of the Ozarks \nthrough the weekend. The ridge will slowly progress eastward, \nbecoming increasingly centered over the forecast area by early to \nmid next week. However, the northern extent of the ridging will be \nsomewhat suppressed by bouts of energy, leading to fairly steady \ntemperature trends through the period.\n\nHigh pressure and associated subsidence will continue to promote \nmostly clear skies and dry weather. The dry air will keep mornings\ncool and afternoons pleasant. Some patchy valley fog will be \npossible each morning, especially near rivers and lakes. Light \nwinds will hinder any notable fire weather concerns despite low \nafternoon RHs.",
